description:
A robot on a grid follows commands. Write the types and functions:

```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
enum Direction { North, East, South, West }

#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq)]
enum Command { Forward(u32), Turn(Turn), Say(String) }

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]
enum Turn { Left, Right }

#[derive(Debug)]
struct Robot { x: i32, y: i32, facing: Direction, log: Vec<String> }

fn parse_command(line: &str) -> Option<Command>
impl Robot {
    fn new() -> Robot                 // at (0, 0) facing North, empty log
    fn apply(&mut self, command: &Command)
}
```

- `parse_command` accepts `forward <n>`, `left`, `right` and `say <text>` (the text is the rest of the line, trimmed and non-empty), ignoring case for the command word; anything else is `None`.
- Moving north is `y + 1`, east `x + 1`, south `y - 1`, west `x - 1`. Turning changes direction by 90 degrees.
- `Say` adds `"(<x>, <y>) <text>"` to the log.

Use `match` for every decision.

